Z||000000||Spyder||03-27-2000||12:23 AM||||Here are some pictures from the Florida Fiero Weekend at Daytona: <BR>This is a small sample of what was there.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f9.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f4.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f5.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f6.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f7.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f8.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Oreif||03-27-2000||12:58 AM||||Thanks for the pics, Wish I could have been there. Here's what my opinions are on the pics. (Pic quality looks really good, was this a film camera or a digital one?)<P>1. The silver GT looks nice!<BR>2. and 3. Don't like the lights on the second one, Looks nice from side. <BR>4. Purple one looks good too. That shade of purple looks nice. Maybe Monkeyman could get that color for his Grape Ape?<BR>5. GT with stripes looks good. <BR>6. I think the orange one would look better if the hood vents were painted the same color as the rest of the body. These headlights look better than the red one above.<BR>7. The "wind-up" key is a good one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>8. OK I give up on this white formula with the "wings are us" look. Sorry it just looks dorky.<BR>9. Interesting Front End looks kinda English style. Sorta like an Austin Martin or Jag. Hope he paints the hood vents when he paints the nose.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||sdm1964||03-27-2000||07:52 AM||||Must be a digital because i have all my film ready to be developed. Spider where were you? I was hoping to meet all the people from the forum that was there. ||||reg||14
Z||000003||bHooper||03-27-2000||08:19 AM||||Thanks for the photo's... the silver GT is beautifull!  I like the car with the stripes, except for the louvers on the qtr windows, and they shoulda carried the stripes onto the rear wing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||03-27-2000||11:01 AM||||I was there on saturday, but didnt run into anyone from the forum.  I also did not see the car with the wind up on the back.  <P>Orief, that front end is a Ferrari look alike that someone of Central Florida Fieros sells.  There were several of those on hand.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||03-27-2000||11:20 AM||||I was there also and only was able to meet Phil from the forum. Too sad. Maybe next time we will have to put some flag or label identifying us. Phil had a little paper flag in his antenna with the forum web site. I have a bookmark so I don't recall the site address but that made me ask him. My red Formula was next to the orange "pumpkin" and behind Phil's yellow SC-3800 Formula.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spyder||03-27-2000||12:46 PM||||I got there kinda late Saturday afternoon. (my plans got changed)<BR>I think a lot of people had cleared out or looking at other cars by the time I was there.<BR>I did talk to one of my friends there with his kit car. (not on the forum) <BR>I didn’t get to stay long because I had already made plans to meet some buddies in Orlando. <BR>Next year name tags, and I’ll bring my car to show.<BR>The camera is a digital.<BR>There were a bunch of neat and Great looking Fieros (to many) and I tried to post the ones that were a little different.<P>You can order CDs with the pics from the show from The Florida Fiero Council (I think): <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2000/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2000/</A> <P>COMING UP:<BR>I will try to go to the Fiero Swap Meet 2000 on April 28th, 29th, &30th (Fri, Sat, Sun): <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spyder||03-27-2000||01:26 PM||||Here are a few more pics:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f1b.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f1a_1.JPG"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||03-27-2000||03:45 PM||||Just a note...<P>The red GT with the Speedcraft banner on the windshield has a Northstar. He used the Design 1 kit and said he would "fix you up" for $10,000 to $15,000. I offered to write him a check and just take his car but, for some reason, he didn't bite. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The yellow car with the hood mod is PHIL's. He said he got the it from RS Motorsports.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Like it!!!<P>Roy L.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000009||sully5||03-27-2000||04:00 PM||||Are the scoops on the yellow car functonal? I saw them on the RSM site and kinda like 'em. ||||reg||5
Z||000010||fiero56||03-27-2000||06:03 PM||||I could have sworn Phil's car was red.||||reg||1
Z||000011||sdm1964||03-27-2000||07:20 PM||||Their is my GT!!!!!! It is the white and black one on the back row, next to the blue one!!!!COOL!!!! The Black 88 GT to the right was to die for. He drove it down from michigan, Looked like brand new. The blue one won best of class in street. I hate HER guts, only kidding, nice coupe only real big metal flakes in paint, not my style||||reg||7
Z||000012||mrfixit58||03-27-2000||09:21 PM||||sully5,<P>Yes, according to PHIL, he noticed salt trails out of the hood this winter.||||reg||1
